# ============================================================================
# VESPERA CITY  (resort city, 28x24 blocks, buffer 1020/1300)  johto_modern
# ============================================================================
# HOOK: Johto's seaside pleasure town that "wakes at dusk": the Colosseum,
#   the Moonlight Theatre, a Game Corner and a row of beach hotels, all
#   strung along the Grand Boulevard that runs from the hills down to the
#   pier. By day it is a sleepy beach town; at night (nite palette) the
#   towers and hotel windows light up, shows start and the Colosseum runs
#   its tournaments. No Gym: the Colosseum is the city's battle draw.
#   Healing is scarce, so the hotels are the rest stops (PC boxes in lobbies).
#
# DISTRICTS / BUILDINGS (door steps in exit lines)
#   Marquee Row (uptown, rows 1-5)
#     Moonlight Theatre (5x4, 7c/7d pillared facade) - shows / contests;
#                         a nightly performance gives a rotating reward
#     Game Corner (4x2), Prize Exchange (1-row shop), Photo Studio (1-row)
#     Fan Club (2x2), Boutique (2x2, outfits / bag colours)
#     Vespera Galleria (3x3 dept store, PCC art), Mart (2x2)
#     Hillside garden (NE): flowers, shrubs, an item
#   Fountain Plaza (centre, rows 6-12)
#     Grand Fountain: fenced 6x4 basin, the boulevard parts around it,
#       planters at its corners, plaza sign; a busker by night
#     Battle Court (W): open-air fenced grass court, gap at the bottom;
#       an Ace Trainer and a referee (practice battles, daily rematch)
#     VESPERA COLOSSEUM (E, 8x5, two-tier roof): the landmark. Weekly
#       tournament / Battle-Tower-lite; locked until N badges
#   Hotel Row (rows 13-16, facing the Strand)
#     Twin Stars Hotel + Twin Stars Casino (silver twin towers; the casino
#       is a second Game Corner floor or a Rocket front)
#     Bellevue Hotel (3x4), Souvenir shop (2x2)
#     Grand Strand Hotel (4x4, the pricey one: full heal + PC + concierge)
#     Seashell Inn (brown 2x2, cheap rest + PC); hotel garden (E)
#   The Strand & Beach (rows 17-23)
#     Brick promenade (W/E exits), railed seawall with gaps to the sand,
#     Beach Cafe, lifeguard hut, rocks, natural 76 shoreline, the Pier
#     (44/46) down the boulevard's axis into the sea
#
# GAMEPLAY BEATS
#   1. Arrive from the N hills straight down the boulevard to the fountain.
#   2. Colosseum guard: "entrants need a Strand Pass". The Grand Strand
#      concierge gives it after you win three Battle Court matches / clear
#      the Fan Club challenge.
#   3. Night: the theatre show (Clefairy/Jigglypuff troupe) and the casino
#      open; something is fixing the tournament -- trail the casino.
#   4. Colosseum tournament (3-4 rounds), prize + repeatable weekly event.
#   5. Post-Surf: sea route S off the pier; hidden items on the beach rocks.
#
# EXITS / CONNECTIONS
#   N  cols 13-14  Grand Boulevard -> hill route
#   W  row 17      the Strand -> coastal route west
#   E  row 17      the Strand -> coastal route east
#   S  sea (rows 21-23): Surf route; Pier tip is a ferry/boat warp if wanted
#
# TILE GAPS / UNCERTAIN BLOCKS
#   - No sand block: the beach is 07/01 path, nearly the same colour.
#   - No beach props (umbrella, palm, deck chair), no ferris wheel/stage.
#   - The Colosseum is a big hall, not an open bowl; 1a's left border
#     shows as a seam beside the door.
#   - 7c/7d (pillar facade) only appear here, not in Goldenrod; check in
#     Polished Map++ that their attributes match.
#   - Galleria reuses the 5f "PCC" sign; reword or redraw.
#   - Fountain rim is unreachable (fenced on all sides), decorative only.
# ============================================================================
tileset johto_modern
ref GoldenrodCity
key T=05 .=01 :=06 ,=02 *=04 h=67 p=07
key ~=35 %=34 $=36 ^=76 (=54 )=55 u=61
key f=41 e=49 r=40 t=42 l=48 j=4a <=44 >=46 s=45 S=77 w=66 x=80 z=81
key R=18 M=1f N=19 A=10 D=17 Z=11 E=1a F=0f O=16 W=1e K=33 H=27 I=23 J=28 1=14 2=13 9=08 0=09 b=2b c=2c
key i=25 k=26 y=29 q=2a d=2d m=2e X=20 Y=24 V=5f L=7c U=7d
key @=2f B=0a
grid:
TTTTTTTTTTTTT::TTTTTTTTTTTTT
TRMMMN:RMMNRN::RNRMN:RN:@*@T
TLUUUU:EFFZOW::OWHIJ:DK:,*,T
TLUUUU:::::::::::XYV::::@,@T
TAFDFZ:1212::::::::::w::,*,T
T:::::w:::::::::::::w::::::T
T:::::::::x::::::z:RMMMMMMNT
Trfffft::::rfffft::MMMMMMMMT
T<,,,,>::::<~~~~>::HIIIIIIJT
T<,,,,>::::<~%~~>::HIIIIIIJT
Tle..ej::::luuuuj::bccEFccZT
T:::::::::x::::::x:::::::::T
T::::w:::w:::::::::w::w::::T
Tikik:RMN@@::::RMMN::::@*@,T
Tyqyq:HIJ,,::::HIIJ::::,@*@T
Tyqyq:HIJRN::::HIIJ::90*,@,T
Tdmdm:ADZOW::::ADFZ::OW,*,*T
::::::::::::::::::::::::::::
eeeeeeeee.eee..eeee.eeeeeeee
pppp12ppppppp..pppppppppppBp
Bp.ppppppppppp..pppppppphppB
